fore line 18\n- Line 9: `unlock()` after line 8\n- Line 19: `unlock()` after line 18\n\nSince both accesses to `myglobal` are protected by the same lock mechanism, there is no atomicity violation. The lock ensures mutual exclusion between the main function and the ISR when accessing the shared variable.\n\nNo defects.\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
